  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Employment creation mainstreamed in national development frameworks.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In September 2021, the Government of Botswana adopted National Employment Policy designed to address the acute labour market challenges besetting the country especially among the youth, women and other groups.
During the biennium, the ILO will work with the National Task Team finalise the NEP Implemntation Plan lead by the Ministry of Labour and Home Affairs. The NEP Implemntation Plan seeks oordinate and guide practical efforts in addressing unemployment and poverty in line with the national development priorities. 
The main objective of the capacity building  is to mainstream quantitative employment impact assessment using economy-wide models as decision tool for employment promotion.</narrative>
  </description>
